Professional Expectations
1. Strong Communication

You’re expected to clearly communicate ideas, updates, and problems—both written (emails, Slack) and verbal (meetings, presentations).

2. Team Collaboration

Work is highly team-based. You’ll need to:

Collaborate across departments (engineering, product, sales)

Respect different roles and perspectives

3. Accountability & Ownership

Employees are expected to:

Take responsibility for their work

Meet deadlines

Fix mistakes proactively without being chased

4. Adaptability

Especially in companies like Wayflyer and Workvivo:

Priorities can change quickly

You must be comfortable learning new tools and processes fast

5. Continuous Learning

In tech-driven environments (like IBM):

You’re expected to keep up with new technologies

Upskilling (courses, certifications) is often encouraged or required

6. Problem-Solving Mindset

Employers expect you to:

Think critically

Suggest solutions, not just highlight problems

Work independently when needed

7. Professionalism & Work Ethics

This includes:

Being punctual and reliable

Respecting deadlines

Maintaining a positive attitude at work

8. Customer/Client Focus

Even in technical roles:

Understand user needs

Deliver value to customers

Maintain high service quality

9. Digital & Technical Competence

You’re expected to be comfortable with:

Workplace tools (e.g. Slack, Jira, cloud platforms)

Data and basic tech systems (even in non-tech roles)

10. Diversity & Inclusion Awareness

Modern Irish companies strongly value:

Respect for different cultures and backgrounds

Inclusive behaviour

Open-minded collaboration

